# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# koris-hub — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local work. Next.js loads `.env` and `.env.local`
# (both git-ignored); nothing here reaches the browser unless it is prefixed
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# The Cloudflare Worker reads `.dev.vars` (at root alongside wrangler.toml)
# in dev, and Worker secrets in production on Cloudflare dashboard.
# See .dev.vars.example.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Build-time (optional) -------------------------------------------------
# Personal access token used by the force-static /api/changelog and
# /api/downloads routes when they call the GitHub Releases API during
# `next build` (src/lib/github-releases.ts). Without it those calls are
# unauthenticated and share GitHub's low per-IP rate limit, which can make the
# build's changelog/downloads data empty. No scopes are needed for public repos.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Cloudflare Worker runtime secrets (documentation only) ----------------
# Set the Jev key in Cloudflare Dashboard under:
# Workers & Pages -> koris-hub -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets -> TYPESAFE_API_KEY
# For local Worker development, put it in .dev.vars (see .dev.vars.example).
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# TYPESAFE_API_BASE=https://api.typesafe.ai
